msgid "Mention people in messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/all-commercial.rst:7
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry, Professional, Enterprise, and "
"Enterprise Advanced plans <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:7
msgid ""
"When you want to get the attention of specific Mattermost users, you can "
"use @mentions. Mattermost supports the following types of @mentions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:9
msgid "`@username <#username>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:10
msgid "`@channel <#channel-and-all>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:11
msgid "`@all <#channel-and-all>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:12
msgid "`@here <#here>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:13
msgid "`@groupname <#groupname>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:14
msgid "`@customusergroupname <#customusergroupname>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:18
msgid ""
"If you forget to mention someone in a message, editing the existing "
"message to add an @mention won't trigger new @mention notifications, "
"desktop notifications, or notification sounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:19
msgid ""
"Mattermost supports mentions for names that include accents (also known "
"as diacritics). Names like Zoë, Jesús, Sørina, François, André, Jokūbas, "
"Siân, KŠthe, or Fañch are returned in autocomplete results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:22
msgid "@username"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:24
msgid ""
"You can mention a teammate by using the *@* symbol plus their username to"
" send them a mention notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:26
msgid ""
"Type *@* or the full-width \"＠\" (U+FF20) to bring up a list of team "
"members who can be mentioned. To filter the list, type the first few "
"letters of any username, first name, last name, or nickname."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:30
msgid ""
"Mattermost v11.3 added support for full-width @, improving the experience"
" for Japanese IME and other international keyboard users. Existing @ "
"mentions are unaffected. See the :doc:v11.3 release notes </product-"
"overview/mattermost-v11-changelog> for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:34
msgid ""
"Using Mattermost in a web browser or the desktop app, you can also press "
"the :kbd:`↑` and :kbd:`↓` arrow keys to scroll through entries in the "
"list, and press :kbd:`ENTER` on Windows or Linux, or :kbd:`↵` on Mac, to "
"select the person to mention. When selected, the username replaces the "
"full name or nickname."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:36
msgid ""
"The following example sends a special mention notification to Alice, "
"whose username is **alice**. The notification alerts her of the channel "
"and message where she was mentioned. If Alice is away from Mattermost and"
" has email notifications turned on, she'll receive an email alert of her "
"mention along with the message text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:42
msgid ""
"If the person you mentioned doesn't belong to the channel or the team, a "
"system message is posted to let you know, and you're given the option to "
"add the person to the channel. You are the only one who can see this "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:45
msgid "@channel and @all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:47
msgid ""
"You can mention an entire channel by typing ``@channel`` or ``@all``. All"
" members of the channel receive a mention notification that behaves the "
"same way as if the members had been mentioned personally. If used in Town"
" Square, it notifies all members of your team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:49
msgid ""
"You can ignore channel-wide mentions in specific channels in the "
"**Channel Menu > Notification Preferences > Ignore mentions for @channel,"
" @here and @all**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:55
#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:66
msgid ""
"If a channel has five or more members, you may be prompted to confirm "
"that you want notifications sent to everyone in the channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:58
msgid "@here"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:60
msgid ""
"You can mention everyone who is online in a channel by typing ``@here``. "
"This sends a desktop notification and push notification to members of the"
" channel who are online. It's counted as a mention in the sidebar. "
"Members who are offline don't receive a notification. When they return to"
" Mattermost they won't see a mention counted in the channel sidebar. "
"Members who are away receive a desktop notification only if they have "
"notifications set to **For all activity**, and they won't see a mention "
"counted in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:68
msgid ""
"You can ignore channel-wide mentions in specific channels by enabling the"
" **Channel Menu > Notification Preferences > Ignore mentions for "
"@channel, @here, and @all** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:71
msgid "@groupname"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/ent-plus.rst:9
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Enterprise and Enterprise Advanced plans"
" <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:76
msgid ""
"This feature enables system admins to configure custom mentions for "
":doc:`LDAP synced groups </administration-guide/onboard/ad-ldap-groups-"
"synchronization>` via the Group Configuration page. This functionality is"
" also supported on the mobile app (from v1.34) if the AD/LDAP groups "
"feature is enabled. The mobile app supports auto-suggesting groups, "
"highlights group member mentions, and also provides a warning dialog when"
" a mention will notify more than five users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:78
msgid ""
"Once enabled for a specific group, users can mention and notify the "
"entire group in a channel (similar to ``@channel`` or ``@all``). Members "
"of the group in that channel will receive a notification. If members of "
"the group mentioned aren't members of the channel, the user who posted "
"the mention is prompted to invite them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:80
msgid ""
"Group mention identifiers (slugs) use the LDAP group name by default. To "
"customize/rename the slug:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:82
msgid "Open **System Console > User Management > Groups**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:83
msgid "Select **Edit** next to the group you want to edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:84
msgid "In **Group Profile > Group Mention** enter the new slug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:85
msgid "Select **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:87
msgid ""
"As with ``@username`` mentions, use *@* to bring up a list of groups that"
" can be mentioned. To filter the list, type the first few letters of any "
"group. Press the :kbd:`↑` and :kbd:`↓` arrow keys to scroll through "
"entries in the list, and then press :kbd:`Enter` on Windows or Linux, or "
"pressing :kbd:`↵` on Mac to select the group you want to mention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:94
msgid "@customusergroupname"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:96
msgid ""
"You can add groups of users to a channel or team by :doc:`creating a "
"custom group </end-user-guide/collaborate/organize-using-custom-user-"
"groups>` and @mentioning that custom group in a channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:98
msgid ""
"Mattermost prompts to you to add any users who aren't already members of "
"that channel to the channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:99
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v9.1, you're given the option to add any users who aren't"
" already members of that team to the team, if you have the permissions to"
" do so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:102
msgid "Words that trigger mentions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:104
msgid ""
"You can customize words that trigger mention notifications in **Settings "
"> Notifications > Words That Trigger Mentions**. By default, you receive "
"mention notifications for your username and for ``@channel``, ``@all`` "
"and ``@here``. You can choose to have your first name be a word that "
"triggers mentions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:106
msgid ""
"You can add a list of customized words to get mention notifications for "
"by typing them into the input box, separated by commas. This is useful if"
" you want to be notified of all posts on certain topics, such as "
"\"interviewing\" or \"marketing\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:109
msgid "See all recent mentions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:111
msgid ""
"Select **@** to the right of the **Search** box to query for your most "
"recent @mentions and words that trigger mentions (excluding LDAP group "
"mentions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:113
msgid "See your most recent @mentions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:116
msgid "Your recent mentions are shown for all of your teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:118
msgid ""
"Select **Jump** next to a search result in the right-hand sidebar to jump"
" the center pane to the channel and location of the message with the "
"mention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:121
msgid "Confirmation dialog warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:123
msgid ""
"When your system admin has configured Mattermost to require confirmations"
" for @mentions, you must confirm any mention that will trigger "
"notifications for more than five users before sending the notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:125
msgid ""
"This confirmation dialog only appears when your system admin has "
"configured this setting in the System Console. See our "
":ref:`configuration settings <administration-guide/configure/site-"
"configuration-settings:show @channel, @all, or @here confirmation "
"dialog>` product documentation for details. This configuration setting is"
" supported on the Mattermost Mobile App (from v1.34) if the :doc:`AD/LDAP"
" groups </administration-guide/onboard/ad-ldap-groups-synchronization>` "
"feature is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:128
msgid "Mention highlights"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:130
msgid ""
"Valid mentions will have highlighted font text with some exceptions, for "
"example if mentions are disabled at the channel level. The highlighted "
"text becomes a hyperlink when a username is displayed. When the username "
"is selected, the profile popover is displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/mention-people.rst:132
msgid ""
"When mentions trigger a notification, the user being notified will see "
"highlighted font text and highlighted font background. This functions as "
"an identifier of which mentions in the post triggered a notification for "
"the user."
msgstr ""

